      "blocks": {
        "q1": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Are waterproof socks good for work boots?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes, and mostly for a reason people do not expect. A safety boot already keeps rain out; what it cannot do is let moisture from the foot escape across a ten-hour shift. A waterproof breathable sock addresses the half the boot cannot.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q2": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What socks do you wear with wellies?",
            "answer": "<p>A waterproof sock is a sensible choice, because wellies have plenty of volume and no breathability at all. Feet get wet inside wellies from the inside far more often than from the outside.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q3": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Will they fit inside safety boots?",
            "answer": "<p>They sit at about the bulk of a thick work sock, so they replace one rather than going over it. Safety boots have a fixed toe cap with no give, so take the larger band if you are between two.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q4": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How long do they last on site?",
            "answer": "<p>Longer than a cheap pair, and shorter than a boot. Abrasion inside a boot and the wrong wash cycle end a waterproof sock long before age does — cool wash, no softener, air dry, and never a tumble dryer or a radiator.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q5": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What are the best socks for standing all day?",
            "answer": "<p>Something that manages moisture rather than just adding padding. Cushioning helps the joints; it does nothing about the fact that a sealed boot keeps a day's worth of moisture against the skin.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "q1",
        "q2",
        "q3",
        "q4",
