    "durability": {
      "type": "content-columns",
      "settings": {
        "color_scheme": "ink",
        "layout": "boxes",
        "numbered": true,
        "eyebrow": "Durability",
        "heading": "Three weeks is not a membrane problem.",
        "lede": "<p>Most cheap waterproof socks do not fail because the membrane is bad. They fail for three reasons, and two of them are fixable.</p>",
        "link_label": "What actually damages a membrane",
        "link_url": "/pages/care-and-washing",
        "mirror": false
      },
      "blocks": {
        "i1": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "There was no membrane to begin with",
            "body": "<p>A great deal of what is sold as waterproof is a treated knit that sheds light rain and then wets through. If a listing does not name a membrane, that is usually why. Ours is Porelle®, licensed, and named on every page.</p>"
          }
        },
        "i2": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "The wear face gave out first",
            "body": "<p>Inside a work boot the abrasion is constant. The outer knit is what takes that, and a thin one wears through to the membrane in weeks. Three layers exist so the middle one is never the wear surface.</p>"
          }
        },
        "i3": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "It went in the tumble dryer",
            "body": "<p>The most common way a waterproof sock dies, and the least discussed. Heat and fabric softener end a laminate far faster than a site does. Cool wash, no softener, air dry.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "i1",
        "i2",
        "i3"
      ]
    },
    "fit": {
      "type": "content-columns",
      "settings": {
        "color_scheme": "paper",
        "layout": "cards",
        "numbered": false,
        "eyebrow": "Fit",
        "heading": "Check the boot before you order.",
        "lede": "<p>Safety boots have a fixed toe cap and no give in it. This is the one thing worth checking before buying.</p>",
        "link_label": "The size bands in centimetres",
        "link_url": "/pages/size-guide",
        "mirror": false
      },
      "blocks": {
        "i1": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Roughly a thick work sock",
            "body": "<p>If you already wear thick socks in your boots, these replace them rather than going over them. If you wear thin socks in a snug boot, allow for the difference.</p>"
          }
        },
        "i2": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Take the larger band if you are between two",
            "body": "<p>A sock that grips the toes inside a steel toe cap is uncomfortable by hour three and shortens the life of the membrane.</p>"
          }
        },
        "i3": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Wellies",
            "body": "<p>No fit problem at all — wellies have volume to spare, which is why a waterproof sock inside a welly is one of the more sensible things you can do with one.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "i1",
        "i2",
        "i3"
      ]
    },
    "warranty": {
      "type": "content-columns",
      "settings": {
        "color_scheme": "wash",
        "layout": "split",
        "numbered": false,
        "eyebrow": "If something goes wrong",
        "heading": "Where you stand.",
        "lede": "<p>On every other page this sits in the footer links. It is here because this is where the decision gets made.</p>",
        "link_label": "The full warranty position",
        "link_url": "/pages/warranty",
        "mirror": false
      },
      "blocks": {
        "i1": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "A fault is not the same as wear",
            "body": "<p>A seam letting water through in the first weeks of normal use is a fault. Thinning at the heel after months on site is wear. We do not charge for returning faulty goods.</p>"
          }
        },
        "i2": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Thirty days to reject outright",
            "body": "<p>Under the Consumer Rights Act 2015 goods must be of satisfactory quality, fit for purpose and as described. Within thirty days of delivery you can reject them for a full refund.</p>"
          }
        },
        "i3": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Six months where the fault is presumed ours",
            "body": "<p>Within six months of delivery, a fault is assumed to have been there from the start unless we can show otherwise.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "i1",
